the target language is: lps.

% Inform Recipe Book, Boston Cream (Goal-Seeking Characters), the first seven
% turns: the player frees the key, opens the case, climbs in and locks it
% from inside; Ogg grows hungry, takes the donuts when the case opens, and
% eats them. Script: open mesh / get key / unlock case / open case /
% enter case / close case / lock case.
%
% Ogg's hunger is the story's own: a counter the turn advances, a growl at 2,
% and from 4 on a plan — fetch something edible, then eat it. The fetch is
% the library's; it opens what is in the way.

the maximum time is 28.

the knowledge base boston cream includes these resources: world, turns.

the actions are:
    *a person* eats *a thing*.
    *a person* growls.

the fluents are:
    the hunger of *a person* is *a number*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is edible.

the knowledge base boston cream includes:

shop is a room.
ogg is a person.
case is a container.
case is openable.
case is lockable.
case is enterable.
case is fixed in place.
basket is a container.
basket is openable.
the key of case is the silver key.
donuts is edible.

initially the turn is 0
    and player is in shop
    and ogg is in shop
    and case is in shop
    and case is closed
    and case is locked
    and donuts is in case
    and basket is in shop
    and basket is closed
    and the silver key is in basket
    and the hunger of ogg is 0.

when the turn begins
then the hunger of ogg that is a number becomes number + 1.

when a person eats a thing
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person eats a thing
then the hunger of the person that is a number becomes 0.

it must not be true that
    a person eats a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the hunger of ogg is 2 at the second time
then ogg growls from the second time to a third time.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the hunger of ogg is a number at the second time
    and the number > 3
    and ogg carries a thing at the second time
    and the thing is edible
then ogg eats the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the hunger of ogg is a number at the second time
    and the number > 3
    and it is not the case that ogg carries donuts at the second time
    and ogg can reach donuts at the second time
then ogg fetches donuts from the second time to a third time.

scenario one is:
    the turn begins from 1 to 2.
    the command is to open basket from 1 to 2.
    the turn ends from 3 to 4.
    the turn begins from 5 to 6.
    the command is to take the silver key from 5 to 6.
    the turn ends from 7 to 8.
    the turn begins from 9 to 10.
    the command is to unlock case with the silver key from 9 to 10.
    the turn ends from 11 to 12.
    the turn begins from 13 to 14.
    the command is to open case from 13 to 14.
    the turn ends from 15 to 16.
    the turn begins from 17 to 18.
    the command is to enter case from 17 to 18.
    the turn ends from 19 to 20.
    the turn begins from 21 to 22.
    the command is to close case from 21 to 22.
    the turn ends from 23 to 24.
    the turn begins from 25 to 26.
    the command is to lock case with the silver key from 25 to 26.
    the turn ends from 27 to 28.
